# Environment for the `spy-der` Vercel project.
#
# Both variables are OPTIONAL. With neither set, the page still renders live
# data: api/proxy.js falls back to reading SPY-DER state through the 0DTE host,
# which publishes it from the same files on the same box. Set
# SPY_DER_DASHBOARD_URL when SPY-DER has a tunnel of its own and the page
# upgrades itself on the next request — no redeploy.

# Reachable base URL of spy-der-dashboard-api (no trailing slash).
#
# That service binds 127.0.0.1:8788, so this has to be a tunnel or reverse
# proxy forwarding to it — never the loopback address itself, which on Vercel
# is the serverless function's own loopback, and never this page's own URL,
# which would make the proxy call itself (rejected with an explanatory 500).
#
#   SPY_DER_DASHBOARD_URL=https://spy-der-api.example.com
#
# Stand one up with, on the VPS — a NAMED tunnel, so the hostname is stable:
#   cloudflared tunnel create spy-der-api
#   cloudflared tunnel route dns spy-der-api spy-der-api.example.com
#   cloudflared tunnel run --url http://127.0.0.1:8788 spy-der-api
#
# Not `cloudflared tunnel --url ...`: that mints a new trycloudflare.com
# hostname on every start, and this value goes stale the first time cloudflared
# restarts. There is no fallback to bridge when that happens — a configured but
# unreachable upstream is a 502 and every panel reads "no data".
#
# 0DTE's tunnel does not work here. It terminates at 127.0.0.1:8765, a different
# process; nothing on that host forwards to 8788.
#
# Unlocks the full /v1 surface: validation, attribution, live Dojo progress,
# pending challengers, and operator Promote / Reject / Rollback.
SPY_DER_DASHBOARD_URL=

# Optional. Only when the URL above sits behind a hop that requires
# Authorization. A direct tunnel to :8788 leaves this unset — reads are open,
# and operator writes travel separately as X-Spy-Der-Operator-Token from the
# browser's paste of SPY_DER_OPERATOR_TOKEN.
DASHBOARD_TOKEN=

# Optional escape hatch: force "native" or "bridge" instead of inferring the
# mode from the URL shape. A URL ending in /api/spy-der is read as the 0DTE hop
# (a read-only adapter that serves published files, not a proxy to :8788);
# anything else is treated as spy-der-dashboard-api itself.
# SPY_DER_DASHBOARD_MODE=
